## Setup

On macOS, install the Xcode Command Line Tools: `xcode-select --install`. The pinned clang finds
the macOS SDK through them.

Install [mise](https://mise.jdx.dev/getting-started.html), for example `brew install mise`. Then
run in the repository:

```sh
mise trust
mise install
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
gh extension install github/gh-stack   # optional: stacked PRs
```

`mise.toml` pins clang, clang-tidy, clang-format, clangd and llvm-cov (one LLVM release from
conda-forge), CMake and Ninja. `mise.lock` pins every download by checksum, for macOS and Linux. The first
install downloads about 1 GB. CI installs the same files. The git hook runs the checks before each
push. `gh stack` is optional: it helps to open and update stacked PRs.

Your editor's clangd must be the pinned one: start the editor from a shell where mise is
activated, or point it at `mise which clangd`.

## Commands

```sh
scripts/check                                  # every quality gate: format, lint, build, test
scripts/format                                 # format every C file
mise exec -- cmake --build --preset dev        # build after scripts/check ran once
mise exec -- ctest --preset dev                # run the tests
build/dev/{{package}}                          # run the program
mise exec -- cmake --preset release && mise exec -- cmake --build --preset release
```

The release build lands in `build/release/`. `scripts/check` is the single list of gates. The git
hook and CI run it too.

